            <ArticleTitle>Unsuspected Metastatic Ovarian Cancer Revealed by 18F-NaF PET/CT Performed to Evaluate Lower-Back Pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>154-156</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/RLU.0000000000001483</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 59-year-old woman with back pain underwent an F-NaF PET/CT bone scan. Unexpectedly, multiple foci of increased tracer uptake were present in the abdomen and pelvis, which corresponded to the calcified soft tissue masses. The subsequent F-FDG PET/CT not only confirmed increased FDG activity in these partially calcified mass but also revealed abnormal activity in noncalcified lesions. The pathological examination demonstrated that the patient had ovarian cancer.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
